A child profile that overrides one of its parent's paths keeps the writes it
says nothing about. Codex applies the parent and then the child, rule by rule,
so `ours` turning `/srv` back to read leaves the workspace roots writable, and
nothing asks.

>>> .codex/config.toml
approval_policy = "never"
default_permissions = "ours"

[permissions.base.filesystem]
"/srv" = "write"

[permissions.base.filesystem.":workspace_roots"]
"." = "write"

[permissions.ours]
extends = "base"

[permissions.ours.filesystem]
"/srv" = "read"
